//! The RAM of a PC-1500 initialized as the manual says after changing the batteries (IM p. 2 and
//! 142): `NEW0` in PRO mode, `NEW` in RESERVE mode, MODE twice (back to PRO) and `OFF`. It is
//! what the ROM itself leaves, from a blank machine (`Pc1500::new_blank`): generated by
//! `tests/boot_state.rs` (`regenerate_the_ram_after_new0`, with `--ignored`), which also checks it
//! is still the ROM's (`the_ram_after_new0_is_the_rom_s`). Do not edit it by hand.
//!
//! The bytes `NEW0` gives a meaning to: BASIC's program empty at `&00C5` (its `&FF`), A-Z
//! (`&7900-&79CF`) and A$-Z$ (`&78C0`, `&7650`, `&7750`) at 0, the reserve area (`&0008-&00C4`) at 0
//! and the system pointers (`&7860-&78BF`). The rest is what the ROM had in its work areas
//! (LCD buffer, stack, input buffer...) when it was switched off.

/// Address of [`SYSTEM_RAM`]'s first byte.
pub(crate) const SYSTEM_RAM_BEGIN: u32 = 0x7600;

